# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A tick span and an unlabelled fence hold wikitext"
# TiddlyWiki hands a code block and a tick span to no parser, so no verdict comes from the reader
# here — the reading answers to what an author writing wikitext shows, and an author showing
# wikitext writes it unlabelled. A label still wins: js stays raw, tw names the base tongue, and
# mem names the memetic dialect, whose own injection paints its sigils where it stands.
#
# A tick opens mid-line, so only the inline rules stand inside it. Handing it the whole grammar let
# a block rule open and swallow the closing tick.
A tick holding `<<amacro>>` and prose.
#               ^^ punctuation.definition.macrocallinline.begin.tiddlywiki5
#                 ^^^^^^ variable.name.macro.tiddlywiki5
#              ^ punctuation.definition.raw.markup.single.begin.tiddlywiki5
#                         ^ punctuation.definition.raw.markup.single.end.tiddlywiki5

```
<$link to="X"/>
#^ punctuation.definition.tag.widget.tiddlywiki5
# ^^^^ entity.name.function.widget.tiddlywiki5
```

```js
var x = 1;
#<- meta.embedded.block.javascript source.js
```

```mem
A macro <<amacro>> stands.
#         ^^^^^^ variable.name.macro.tiddlywiki5
```

# A tick matches on one line rather than opening a region: where no end pattern matches, TextMate
# runs to the end of the document, and an unterminated `<<` inside a tick took the rest of the
# file. The parser says the same — codeinline.js records `unterminated-codeinline` and renders the
# delimiter as literal text, which a rule that fails to match spells exactly. An element, a style
# run and a nested tick each swallowed past the closing backtick; each now reads as raw content.
An element `<svg width="1">` names itself.
#           ^^^^ markup.raw.inline.tiddlywiki5
A style run `@@color:red;` and a tick after it `x`.
#            ^^^^^^^^^^^^ markup.raw.inline.tiddlywiki5
#                                               ^ markup.raw.inline.tiddlywiki5

An ordinary sentence stands here.
#<- meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5

An unterminated `tick stands as prose.
#<- meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5
#               ^ meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5

An ordinary sentence stands after it.
#<- meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5
